Package: geneticumap
Title: Evolutionary Algorithm for UMAP-based Clustering Pipeline Parameter Optimization for Single-Cell RNA-Seq Data
Version: 0.99.2
Date: 2026-09-25
Authors@R: c(
    person("Lisa-Maria", "Winter", email = "lisa-maria-1.winter@uni-ulm.de", role = c("aut")),
    person("Hanna", "Wagner", email = "hanna.wagner@uni-ulm.de", role = c("aut")),
    person("Dominik", "Dreiheller", role = c("aut")),
    person("Hans A.", "Kestler", email = "hans.kestler@uni-ulm.de", role = c("cre")))
Description: The geneticumap package searches for single-cell clustering parameters by treating the Seurat preprocessing and clustering workflow
    as an optimization problem. The UMAP-based clustering pipeline parameters for single-cell RNA-seq data (like resolution, number of PCs, or neighbor counts)
    evolve using an evolutionary algorithm to systematically search for an optimal set of parameters for a given dataset.
    The most appropriate configuration is objectively identified by the Calinski-Harabasz index.
    The package is developed at the [Institute of Medical Systems Biology of Ulm University](https://sysbio.uni-ulm.de).
